  "term": "interpretive therapy",
  "definition": "Interpretive therapy is a Freudian form of psychotherapy that looks at the meaning of a person’s words, dreams, and interactions in relation to everyday life. It has also been described by some mental health professionals as helpful in shaping treatment approaches for chronic pain and pain syndromes.",
